From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy Whitcroft <apw@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 3 May 2012 16:01:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: (no-up) kconfig: in debug mode some 0 length
 message prints occur

Has no real kernel impact, so continue to carry.

When we enable the zconfdump() debugging we see assertion failures
attempting to print the config.  Convert this into a noop.

Signed-off-by: Andy Whitcroft <apw@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00008
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@cf20888a0af4f636358e4d4b5bfc19ae238678bb
---
 scripts/kconfig/lkc.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/kconfig/lkc.h b/scripts/kconfig/lkc.h
index 7e6f6ca299cf..68ab0fd38c45 100644
--- a/scripts/kconfig/lkc.h
+++ b/scripts/kconfig/lkc.h
@@ -44,7 +44,9 @@ const char *conf_get_configname(void);
 /* confdata.c and expr.c */
 static inline void xfwrite(const void *str, size_t len, size_t count, FILE *out)
 {
-	assert(len != 0);
+	//assert(len != 0);
+	if (len == 0)
+		return;
 
 	if (fwrite(str, len, count, out) != count)
 		fprintf(stderr, "Error in writing or end of file.\n");
